  "summary": "I am a graduate of the University of Texas at Dallas with a Bachelors Degree in Computer Engineering.\n\nSoftware Verification & Validation / Embedded Software Engineer with nearly 4 years of experience developing and verifying FDA Class II medical device software. Strong background in embedded C++ development on STM32, alarm and display management, Python-based automation, and full V&V lifecycle execution including usability engineering, risk management, and 510(k) support. Experienced working in a waterfall medical device environment with phase gates, while supporting agile sprint-based software development. Proven collaborator across R&D, QA, and Regulatory teams. \n\nIn my free times I enjoy Bouldering and Hiking and just traveling and seeing new places and people and just growing my skill sets and learning new ones over time.\n\nI am confident in my ability to adapt and thrive in any professional environment through my experience with customer service, volunteerism, and my professional experience",
